LIB_LOAD("jp",{"jp1":{"challenge":[{"q":"In which year was John Ploughman's Talk written?","o":["1869","1678","1915","1722"],"why":"By C. H. Spurgeon."},{"q":"Who did Spurgeon write it for?","o":["Ordinary working people","Only preachers","Only kings","Only scientists"],"why":"In plain, funny language."},{"q":"What's the name of the farm lad in our story?","o":["Will","Larry","Tom","John"],"why":"He learns from John."},{"q":"Which insect works without anyone telling it to?","o":["The ant","The fly","The mosquito","The butterfly"],"why":"Go to the ant!"},{"q":"What do idle hands lead to, according to John?","o":["Mischief","Wisdom","Wealth","Rest"],"why":"The devil's playground."},{"q":"Who catches the worm?","o":["The early bird","The late bird","The sleepy bird","The lazy cat"],"why":"Rise early!"},{"q":"Who did John say to give the first part of your day to?","o":["God","Friends","TV","Nobody"],"why":"Before the noise starts."},{"q":"How did Will feel after his first crooked furrow?","o":["He wanted to give up","Proud","Sleepy","Hungry"],"why":"Until he tried again."},{"q":"What did John say about every master?","o":["They were once a beginner who didn't give up","They were born perfect","They never practised","They had luck"],"why":"Rome wasn't built in a day."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Go to the ant, thou ___.\"","o":["sluggard","farmer","child","king"],"why":"Proverbs 6:6."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What did John say his first furrow looked like?","o":["A drunken caterpillar walked across the field","A perfect line","A rainbow","A river"],"why":"Every master starts somewhere!"},"choices":[{"title":"Homework time","q":"You have homework due tomorrow, but your favourite show is on. You're tempted to do it 'later'.","o":[{"t":"Do the homework first, then enjoy the show.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like the ant, do the work first, without being pushed."},{"t":"Watch the show and copy someone's homework in the morning.","f":"That's Lazy Larry's way."},{"t":"Do half and forget the rest.","f":"Finish what you start."}]},{"title":"Morning alarm","q":"Your alarm goes off for an early study session you planned. Your bed is warm and cosy.","o":[{"t":"Get up, splash water on your face, and start with a short prayer.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Love not sleep, lest you come to poverty."},{"t":"Press snooze five times.","f":"Snooze steals your morning."},{"t":"Turn the alarm off for good.","f":"That's giving up before you start."}]},{"title":"First failure","q":"You tried out for the school choir and didn't get in. You want to never sing again.","o":[{"t":"Ask how to improve, keep practising, and try again next time.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Try, then try again. Fall seven times, rise eight."},{"t":"Quit singing forever.","f":"One 'no' isn't the end."},{"t":"Say the judges were unfair.","f":"Look forward, not back."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of John Ploughman's Talk in real life."},{"sc":"anthill","n":"🐜 Work like the ant: do your jobs without needing to be pushed."},{"sc":"farm","n":"🐓 Make the most of mornings, and give the first part of your day to God."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"🔁 Try, then try again. Keep your eyes on the goal, not your mistakes."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"🌾 Every master was once a beginner who didn't give up."}],"stops":{"jp1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"In 1869, the famous preacher C. H. Spurgeon wrote a very different kind of book. He didn't write it as a preacher. He wrote it as a farm worker called {John Ploughman}."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"Why? Because he wanted ordinary working people, farmers, labourers, shopkeepers and their children, to enjoy reading it. So he wrote the way they talked: plainly, wisely and with lots of jokes."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"Morning, young 'un! I'm John Ploughman. I've spent my life behind a plough, and I've picked up a few bits of sense along the way. Want to hear some?"},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"will","e":"smile","t":"Yes please, Mr Ploughman! My name's Will. Are you going to preach at me?"},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Bless you, no! I'm only a {ploughman}. I'll just tell you what I've learned from the fields, the animals and the Good Book."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"John Ploughman's talk is full of {proverb}s: short, wise sayings. In this book, we'll put them side by side with Nigerian proverbs, because wisdom sounds the same in every language."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"A wise saying is like a nail. Drive it in well, and you can hang a lot on it."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"So pull up a hay bale and listen. John Ploughman has a lot to say about work, money, words and home."}],"quote":{"text":"The proverbs of Solomon the son of David, king of Israel; to know wisdom and instruction; to perceive the words of understanding.","who":"Proverbs 1:1-2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Wisdom is for everyone","text":"Spurgeon wrote John Ploughman's Talk so that everyday people could understand it. Wisdom isn't just for clever professors. It's for farmers, traders, students and you. The book of Proverbs was written to make ordinary people wise."},"think":"What's your favourite wise saying, from your parents, grandparents or the Bible? Why do you remember it?","proverb":{"text":"Ọmọdé gbọ́n, àgbà gbọ́n, la fi dá Ilé-Ifẹ̀.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"The young were wise and the old were wise: that is how Ile-Ife was built. Wisdom belongs to everyone."},"quiz":[{"q":"Who really wrote John Ploughman's Talk?","o":["C. H. Spurgeon","John Bunyan","A real farmer","Mary Slessor"],"why":"In 1869."},{"q":"Why did he write as a ploughman?","o":["So ordinary working people would enjoy it","He was tired of preaching","He wanted to be a farmer","By accident"],"why":"Plain, wise and funny."},{"q":"What is a proverb?","o":["A short, wise saying","A long story","A kind of plough","A song"],"why":"People repeat them because they're true."},{"q":"What did John say a wise saying is like?","o":["A nail you can hang a lot on","A heavy stone","A cloud","A cake"],"why":"Drive it in well."},{"q":"According to Proverbs 1:7, what is the beginning of knowledge?","o":["The fear of the LORD","Money","School","Age"],"why":"Fools despise wisdom."}]},"jp1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"farm","w":"idleman","e":"sleep","t":"Zzz... Wake me when lunch is ready..."},{"sc":"farm","w":"will","e":"smirk","t":"Mr Ploughman, Larry's been asleep under that tree since breakfast."},{"sc":"farm","w":"ploughman","e":"stern","t":"Aye. Lazy Larry. He'd sleep through the end of the world if it came before dinner."},{"sc":"farm","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Idle hands are the devil's playground, Will. A lazy man doesn't just do nothing. He usually ends up doing mischief."},{"sc":"anthill","n":"John took Will to the edge of the field. There was an anthill, busy with hundreds of tiny ants, each carrying a crumb or a seed."},{"sc":"anthill","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"Look at these little workers. No boss shouting at them. No one paying them. But they work all summer, storing food for winter."},{"sc":"anthill","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"King Solomon said it three thousand years ago: 'Go to the ant, thou sluggard; consider her ways, and be wise.'"},{"sc":"anthill","w":"will","e":"big","t":"So a lazy person can learn from an ant!"},{"sc":"anthill","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Exactly. If an ant can do its work without being told, so can you."}],"quote":{"text":"Go to the ant, thou sluggard; consider her ways, and be wise: which having no guide, overseer, or ruler, provideth her meat in the summer.","who":"Proverbs 6:6-8","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Work without being pushed","text":"The ant works hard with no boss watching. John Ploughman says laziness never stays harmless: idle hands find trouble. Do your work, chores and homework without needing someone to push you."},"think":"Which of your jobs or chores do you only do when someone pushes you? How could you be more like the ant?","proverb":{"text":"Iṣẹ́ ni oògùn ìṣẹ́.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"Hard work is the cure for poverty."},"quiz":[{"q":"What was Lazy Larry doing?","o":["Sleeping under a tree","Ploughing","Feeding the animals","Reading"],"why":"Since breakfast!"},{"q":"What does John say about idle hands?","o":["They're the devil's playground","They're relaxed","They're clean","They're strong"],"why":"Laziness leads to mischief."},{"q":"What creature did Solomon tell the lazy to learn from?","o":["The ant","The lion","The donkey","The eagle"],"why":"Proverbs 6:6."},{"q":"What's special about how ants work?","o":["Nobody has to make them work","They only work at night","They get paid","They work alone"],"why":"No guide, overseer or ruler."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb 'Iṣẹ́ ni oògùn ìṣẹ́' teach?","o":["Hard work is the cure for poverty","Rest is best","Work is bad","Ants are lazy"],"why":"Like the ant."}]},"jp1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"farm","n":"Early in the morning, before the sun was fully up, John Ploughman was already harnessing his horses."},{"sc":"farm","w":"will","e":"sleep","t":"Mr Ploughman... it's still nearly dark... why are you up so early?"},{"sc":"farm","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"Because the early bird catches the worm, lad! The farmer who lies in bed late never ploughs his field on time."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"The cool morning is the best time to work. By noon, the sun is hot and the day is half gone. A late riser runs after his work all day long and never catches it."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"John Ploughman loved to say that he who wants to thrive must rise early. But it isn't only about farm work."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Get up early for God too, Will. Give him the first of your day, before the noise starts. Then everything goes better."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"But I like my bed..."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"So does Larry! Look where it's got him. Love not sleep, lest you come to poverty!"}],"quote":{"text":"Love not sleep, lest thou come to poverty; open thine eyes, and thou shalt be satisfied with bread.","who":"Proverbs 20:13","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Make the most of mornings","text":"John Ploughman says the early riser gets ahead. Mornings are fresh and quiet. Use them for your work and especially for God. Rest is good, but don't let too much sleep steal your day."},"think":"What could you do with an extra twenty minutes in the morning, before school?","quiz":[{"q":"Why was John up so early?","o":["The early bird catches the worm","He couldn't sleep","It was a holiday","The cow woke him"],"why":"Farmers who lie in late fall behind."},{"q":"Why is the morning the best time to work on a farm?","o":["It's cool, before the hot noon sun","It's darker","Animals are asleep","It's not"],"why":"By noon the day is half gone."},{"q":"What else did John say to give the first of your day to?","o":["God","Your phone","TV","Sleep"],"why":"Before the noise starts."},{"q":"What does Proverbs 20:13 warn?","o":["Love not sleep, lest you come to poverty","Sleep all day","Never sleep","Sleep makes you rich"],"why":"Open thine eyes."},{"q":"What does John say happens to someone who gets up late?","o":["He runs after his work all day and never catches it","He gets rich","He is never tired","Nothing"],"why":"Rise early!"}]},"jp1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"One day Will tried to drive the plough himself. The horses pulled the wrong way. The furrow came out crooked as a snake."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"will","e":"frown","t":"It's no good! I'll never plough a straight line. I give up!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Give up? After one crooked furrow? Lad, my first furrow looked like a drunken caterpillar walked across the field!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"There's a little word that every boy and girl should know: TRY. And when you've tried, try again."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Keep your eye fixed on a point at the far end of the field, and don't keep looking back. That's the secret of a straight furrow."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"Will tried again. And again. The fifth furrow was nearly straight."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"will","e":"big","t":"Look, Mr Ploughman! It's straight! Well, almost!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"There! Rome wasn't built in a day, and neither is a ploughman. Every master was once a beginner who didn't give up."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"Jesus said something similar: no one who puts his hand to the plough and keeps looking back is fit for God's kingdom. Keep looking forward, and keep going."}],"quote":{"text":"For a just man falleth seven times, and riseth up again.","who":"Proverbs 24:16","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Fall seven, rise eight","text":"Will's first furrow was crooked, and he wanted to quit. John Ploughman says: try, then try again. Keep your eyes on the goal, not on your mistakes behind you. Every expert started as a beginner who didn't give up."},"think":"What's something you gave up on too quickly? Could you try it again this week?","proverb":{"text":"Bí ọmọdé bá ṣubú, á wo iwájú.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"When a child falls, he looks forward. Don't dwell on your fall; get up and move ahead."},"quiz":[{"q":"What happened to Will's first furrow?","o":["It came out crooked","It was perfect","The plough broke","It rained"],"why":"Crooked as a snake!"},{"q":"What little word did John say everyone should know?","o":["TRY","STOP","SLEEP","QUIT"],"why":"And when you've tried, try again."},{"q":"What's the secret of a straight furrow?","o":["Fix your eye on a point ahead and don't look back","Close your eyes","Go very fast","Look at your feet"],"why":"Eyes on the goal."},{"q":"Which furrow was nearly straight?","o":["The fifth","The first","None","The hundredth"],"why":"He kept trying."},{"q":"According to Proverbs 24:16, what does a just man do when he falls?","o":["Rises up again","Stays down","Blames others","Runs away"],"why":"Seven times!"}]}}},"jp2":{"challenge":[{"q":"What was Flashy Fred's problem?","o":["He spent every penny at once","He worked too hard","He saved too much","He was too kind"],"why":"Always broke by Monday."},{"q":"What is John's simple money rule?","o":["Spend a little less than you get","Spend all you get","Borrow when you need","Never earn"],"why":"Earn ten, spend nine."},{"q":"What should you ask before buying something?","o":["Do I need it, or just want it?","What colour is it?","Is it popular?","Can I borrow for it?"],"why":"Needs first."},{"q":"What did John say debt is like?","o":["A rope round your neck","A friend","A holiday","A gift"],"why":"It gets tighter."},{"q":"What does Proverbs 22:7 say the borrower is?","o":["Servant to the lender","Master of the lender","Free","Rich"],"why":"Debt takes away freedom."},{"q":"What is thrift?","o":["Being careful with money, not wasting it","Being mean","Being lazy","Being rich"],"why":"Wise saving."},{"q":"What did Will's savings pay for?","o":["His mother's medicine","A party","Fred's debts","New boots"],"why":"Little by little."},{"q":"What did John say about pennies and pounds?","o":["Look after the pennies, and the pounds look after themselves","Pennies are worthless","Spend pennies first","Pounds are better"],"why":"Small adds up."},{"q":"What makes a man rich, according to John?","o":["A happy heart","Money","Horses","Boots"],"why":"Contentment."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Owe no man any thing, but to ___ one another.\"","o":["love","pay","help","lend"],"why":"Romans 13:8."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What did John say is better than rising in debt?","o":["Going to bed without supper","Borrowing from a friend","Asking the squire","Selling your boots"],"why":"If you can't pay for it, do without it."},"choices":[{"title":"Birthday money","q":"You receive ₦10,000 for your birthday. Your friends say you should spend it all on snacks and data this weekend.","o":[{"t":"Make a plan: give some, save some, and enjoy spending some.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Spend a little less than you get, and you'll always have something."},{"t":"Spend it all this weekend.","f":"That's Flashy Fred's way."},{"t":"Lend it all to friends who never pay back.","f":"Kindness is good, but be wise too."}]},{"title":"Buy now, pay later","q":"An older friend offers to lend you money to buy an expensive pair of trainers. You'd pay her back with interest over three months.","o":[{"t":"Say no thanks. Save up and buy them when you can afford them, or choose something cheaper.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! If you can't pay for it, do without it."},{"t":"Borrow it. You'll figure out how to pay later.","f":"Debt is a rope that gets tighter."},{"t":"Borrow it and avoid her afterwards.","f":"That's breaking your word too."}]},{"title":"Comparing","q":"A classmate shows off a brand-new phone. You suddenly feel your phone is rubbish.","o":[{"t":"Be happy for them, and thank God for what you have.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Godliness with contentment is great gain."},{"t":"Nag your parents until they buy you one.","f":"Contentment brings more joy than things."},{"t":"Say mean things about their phone.","f":"Jealousy makes everyone poorer."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"market","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of John Ploughman's Talk in real life."},{"sc":"market","n":"👛 Spend a little less than you get. Ask: need or want?"},{"sc":"market","n":"⛓️ Avoid debt. If you can't pay for it, do without it."},{"sc":"barns","n":"🐷 Save a little, often. Thrift lets you bless others."},{"sc":"meadow","n":"😌 Be content. A happy heart is richer than a full purse."}],"stops":{"jp2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"market","n":"It was market day. Will had just been paid for a week's work on the farm, and his pocket was jingling."},{"sc":"market","w":"spendthrift","e":"big","t":"Will! Come on! Sweets, a new cap, a ribbon for your sister, and a pie! You only live once!"},{"sc":"market","n":"Flashy Fred spent every penny the moment he got it. By Monday, he was always broke and borrowing from someone."},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Hold on, Will. Before you spend, let me tell you a farmer's secret."},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"Always spend a little less than you get. If you earn ten pennies and spend nine, you're a rich man. If you earn ten and spend eleven, you're a poor man, however much you earn."},{"sc":"market","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"But I want nice things too!"},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Nothing wrong with nice things, lad, once you've paid for what you need and put a little by. A wise man asks: do I need it, or do I just want it?"},{"sc":"market","n":"Will bought what he needed, a small treat, and saved the rest. Fred laughed at him. By Thursday, Fred was asking Will to lend him money."}],"quote":{"text":"There is treasure to be desired and oil in the dwelling of the wise; but a foolish man spendeth it up.","who":"Proverbs 21:20","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Spend less than you get","text":"John Ploughman's simple rule: spend a little less than you receive, and you'll be all right. Before you buy, ask: do I need it, or just want it? Flashy spending looks fun on Saturday and feels terrible by Thursday."},"think":"Next time you get some money, what's your plan? How much would you save, spend and give?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Flashy Fred do with his money?","o":["Spent every penny at once","Saved it all","Gave it away","Lost it"],"why":"By Monday he was broke."},{"q":"What was John's farmer's secret?","o":["Spend a little less than you get","Spend more than you get","Never spend anything","Borrow a lot"],"why":"Earn ten, spend nine."},{"q":"What question does a wise person ask before buying?","o":["Do I need it, or just want it?","Is it shiny?","Is it expensive?","Do my friends have it?"],"why":"Needs before wants."},{"q":"What happened to Fred by Thursday?","o":["He asked Will to lend him money","He became rich","He opened a shop","Nothing"],"why":"Foolish spending."},{"q":"What does Proverbs 21:20 say a foolish man does?","o":["Spends it up","Saves it","Gives it","Hides it"],"why":"The wise have treasure."}]},"jp2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"market","w":"spendthrift","e":"worried","t":"Will, lend me five pennies till Saturday? I owe the baker, and the cobbler, and the butcher..."},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"stern","t":"Fred, lad, you're tying yourself up in knots. {Debt} is like a rope round your neck. Every day it gets a bit tighter."},{"sc":"market","n":"John Ploughman hated debt. He said that when you owe money, you aren't really free. You're afraid to meet the people you owe. You can't sleep. You can't look people in the eye."},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"When you borrow, you often have to pay back more than you borrowed. That extra is called {interest}. The debt grows while you sleep."},{"sc":"market","w":"shopkeeper","e":"frown","t":"Fred! You still owe me for last month's bread!"},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"Better to go to bed without supper than to rise in debt. If you can't pay for it, do without it!"},{"sc":"market","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"So I shouldn't lend Fred the money?"},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Help him, by all means, if you can afford to give it. But help him most by teaching him what you've learned: don't spend what you don't have."},{"sc":"market","n":"The Bible doesn't say borrowing is always wrong. But it warns that 'the borrower is servant to the lender', and teaches us to owe no one anything except love."}],"quote":{"text":"The rich ruleth over the poor, and the borrower is servant to the lender.","who":"Proverbs 22:7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Debt is a chain","text":"John Ploughman called debt a rope that gets tighter every day. If you can't pay for it, do without it. Being debt-free means being free: free to sleep, free to look people in the eye, and free to give."},"think":"Why do you think the Bible says the borrower becomes like a servant to the lender?","quiz":[{"q":"What did John compare debt to?","o":["A rope round your neck that gets tighter","A warm blanket","A gift","A song"],"why":"Every day it gets tighter."},{"q":"What is interest?","o":["Extra money you pay back on top of what you borrowed","A hobby","A kind of bread","A bank holiday"],"why":"The debt grows while you sleep."},{"q":"What did John say is better than rising in debt?","o":["Going to bed without supper","Borrowing more","Hiding","Running away"],"why":"If you can't pay, do without."},{"q":"How did John say to help Fred most?","o":["Teach him not to spend what he doesn't have","Lend him everything","Laugh at him","Ignore him"],"why":"Help with wisdom."},{"q":"What does Romans 13:8 say we should owe each other?","o":["Only love","Money","Gifts","Favours"],"why":"Owe no man any thing, but to love."}]},"jp2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"barns","n":"In the barn, John Ploughman showed Will a big heap of grain."},{"sc":"barns","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"How do you think this heap got here, Will?"},{"sc":"barns","w":"will","e":"big","t":"Somebody tipped it in all at once?"},{"sc":"barns","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"No! Sack by sack. Handful by handful. That's how you build anything worth having: little by little."},{"sc":"barns","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Look after the pennies, and the pounds will look after themselves. A few coins put away every week become a good store over a year."},{"sc":"barns","n":"Will started keeping a small box. Every week, he put in a little of his pay. He didn't touch it, even when he wanted to."},{"sc":"barns","n":"Months later, when his mother needed medicine and there was no money in the house, Will opened his box. There was enough."},{"sc":"barns","w":"will","e":"big","t":"Mother! I've got it! I saved it little by little!"},{"sc":"barns","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"That's {thrift}, lad. Not meanness, but wisdom. And now you've been able to bless someone with it."}],"quote":{"text":"Wealth gotten by vanity shall be diminished: but he that gathereth by labour shall increase.","who":"Proverbs 13:11","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Save a little, often","text":"John Ploughman's grain heap was built handful by handful. Saving works the same way: a little, regularly, adds up. Thrift isn't being mean. It means being ready to help when needs come."},"think":"If you saved just a small amount every week for a year, what good could it do?","proverb":{"text":"Sannu sannu bata hana zuwa.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"Going slowly does not stop you from arriving. Little by little, you get there."},"quiz":[{"q":"How did the heap of grain get into the barn?","o":["Sack by sack, handful by handful","All at once","By magic","It grew there"],"why":"Little by little."},{"q":"What did John say about pennies?","o":["Look after the pennies, and the pounds look after themselves","Throw them away","Pennies don't matter","Spend them first"],"why":"Small amounts add up."},{"q":"What did Will do every week?","o":["Put a little of his pay in a box","Spent it all","Gave it to Fred","Hid it in the field"],"why":"He didn't touch it."},{"q":"How did Will's savings help?","o":["He paid for his mother's medicine","He bought a horse","He went on holiday","They didn't"],"why":"Thrift blesses others."},{"q":"What does the Hausa proverb mean?","o":["Going slowly doesn't stop you arriving","Run fast","Never travel","Stay home"],"why":"Little by little."}]},"jp2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"meadow","n":"One evening, Will and John sat on a gate, watching the sun go down over the fields."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"Mr Ploughman, the squire's son has a fine horse and new boots. I wish I had what he has."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Ah, Will. If you're always looking at what other people have, you'll never enjoy what you've got."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"A man who isn't {content} with a little will never be content with a lot. Riches don't make a happy heart. A happy heart makes a man rich."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"I've got a roof over my head, bread on my table, a Bible on my shelf and a God in heaven who loves me. What more does a ploughman need?"},{"sc":"meadow","n":"Will thought about it. He had a loving mother, good work, friends, and a God who cared for him. Suddenly, the squire's son's boots didn't matter so much."},{"sc":"meadow","w":"will","e":"big","t":"I suppose I'm richer than I thought!"},{"sc":"meadow","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"That's the spirit! Godliness with contentment is great gain. Now, let's go and have our supper."}],"quote":{"text":"But godliness with contentment is great gain. For we brought nothing into this world, and it is certain we can carry nothing out.","who":"1 Timothy 6:6-7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Rich in what matters","text":"Comparing yourself with others steals your joy. John Ploughman says a contented heart is richer than a full purse. Count your blessings: people, provision and, most of all, God's love."},"think":"Make a list of five things you're thankful for right now. How does it change how you feel?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Will wishing for?","o":["What the squire's son had","A new plough","More sleep","Nothing"],"why":"A fine horse and new boots."},{"q":"What does always looking at others' things do?","o":["Stops you enjoying what you have","Makes you rich","Makes you wise","Nothing"],"why":"Comparison steals joy."},{"q":"What did John say makes a man rich?","o":["A happy heart","Lots of money","Fine boots","A big house"],"why":"Not the other way round."},{"q":"What did John list as all a ploughman needs?","o":["A roof, bread, a Bible and God's love","A palace","Gold","Fame"],"why":"Contentment."},{"q":"What is 'great gain' according to 1 Timothy 6:6?","o":["Godliness with contentment","Wealth","Fame","Power"],"why":"We brought nothing in."}]}}},"jp3":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Mrs Chatterbox spread?","o":["Gossip","Butter","Seeds","Kindness"],"why":"Half of it untrue."},{"q":"A dog that will fetch a bone will...?","o":["Carry a bone","Bury a bone","Eat a bone","Lose a bone"],"why":"Gossips gossip about you too."},{"q":"What happens when there is no wood?","o":["The fire goes out","The fire grows","It snows","Nothing"],"why":"Proverbs 26:20."},{"q":"What did John say about the loudest drum?","o":["It's the emptiest","It's the strongest","It's the smallest","It's the best"],"why":"Tall talk is hollow."},{"q":"Who got Bill's cart out of the mud?","o":["A quiet old farmer","Big Bragging Bill","Mrs Chatterbox","Grumpy Gus"],"why":"Doers say less."},{"q":"What should praise you, according to Proverbs 27:2?","o":["Another person","Your own mouth","A newspaper","Nobody"],"why":"Not your own lips."},{"q":"Who did Will help on Saturday?","o":["Widow Jones","Big Bill","Grumpy Gus","The squire"],"why":"He kept his word."},{"q":"What did Will get for keeping his word?","o":["Apple cake and a better job offer","Nothing","A telling-off","A horse"],"why":"Trust opens doors."},{"q":"What did John suggest instead of grumbling?","o":["Thanking God","Shouting","Sulking","Running away"],"why":"A thankful heart."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Let your communication be, Yea, yea; ___, nay.\"","o":["Nay","Maybe","Perhaps","Sometimes"],"why":"Matthew 5:37."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! According to the Yoruba proverb, words are like what?","o":["Eggs: once dropped, they break","Feathers","Rocks","Rain"],"why":"Ẹyin lọ̀rọ̀."},"choices":[{"title":"Juicy gossip","q":"A classmate whispers, \"Want to hear something about Tolu? Promise not to tell!\"","o":[{"t":"Say kindly, \"I'd rather not. It's not my business.\"","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Let gossip stop with you. Take away the wood."},{"t":"Listen, but don't repeat it.","f":"Listening still adds wood to the fire."},{"t":"Listen and tell three more people.","f":"Words are like eggs: they break and can't be put back."}]},{"title":"Showing off","q":"You came first in a maths competition. You feel like posting about it all day and telling everyone how clever you are.","o":[{"t":"Thank God, share the news simply, and let others do the praising.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Let another man praise thee, not thine own mouth."},{"t":"Brag non-stop.","f":"Tall talk is a balloon waiting for a pin."},{"t":"Mock those who didn't win.","f":"That's both boasting and unkindness."}]},{"title":"A small promise","q":"You promised your little sister you'd play a game with her after school. Now your friends want you online.","o":[{"t":"Keep your promise to your sister first.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! If you say yes, mean yes."},{"t":"Tell her 'maybe tomorrow' and go online.","f":"Broken small promises teach people not to trust you."},{"t":"Play for one minute, then leave.","f":"Keep the spirit of the promise, not just the letter."}]},{"title":"Rainy day moan","q":"It's raining on the day of your class trip, and everyone is moaning loudly.","o":[{"t":"Look for something good: make the best of it and encourage others.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! A thankful heart finds something good in every day."},{"t":"Grumble louder than everyone.","f":"Grumbling never stopped the rain."},{"t":"Sulk all day.","f":"You'll miss the fun that's still possible."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"market","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of John Ploughman's Talk in real life."},{"sc":"market","n":"🥚 Words are eggs. Let gossip stop with you."},{"sc":"farm","n":"🎈 No tall talk. Let your work speak and others praise you."},{"sc":"barns","n":"🤝 Keep your word. Yes means yes."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"🌤️ Swap grumbling for thanking."}],"stops":{"jp3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"market","w":"gossip","e":"big","t":"Have you heard? The miller's wife bought a new hat, and I know where she got the money from! Don't tell anyone I said so..."},{"sc":"market","n":"Mrs Chatterbox knew everybody's business, and she told it to everybody else. Half of what she said wasn't even true."},{"sc":"market","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"Mr Ploughman, she tells me secrets about everyone. Is that bad?"},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"stern","t":"Will, there's an old saying: a dog that will fetch a bone will carry a bone. If she brings you gossip about others, she'll carry gossip about you to them too!"},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"{Gossip} is like a fire. One spark, and the whole village is burning. But take away the wood, and the fire goes out."},{"sc":"market","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"So be the person who doesn't add wood. When gossip comes to you, let it stop with you."},{"sc":"market","n":"Next time Mrs Chatterbox started a story, Will politely changed the subject. She soon stopped telling him things. And Will's friends knew they could trust him."}],"quote":{"text":"Where no wood is, there the fire goeth out: so where there is no talebearer, the strife ceaseth.","who":"Proverbs 26:20","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Let gossip stop with you","text":"John Ploughman warns: someone who gossips to you will gossip about you. Gossip spreads like fire, but it goes out when there's no wood. Be the person gossip can't pass through. People will trust you."},"think":"Why do you think people who refuse to gossip become the most trusted friends?","proverb":{"text":"Ẹyin lọ̀rọ̀; bó bá bọ́, fífọ́ ní í fọ́.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"Words are like eggs: once they fall, they break. You can't take back what you've said."},"quiz":[{"q":"What did Mrs Chatterbox do?","o":["Told everybody's business to everybody else","Kept secrets","Helped the poor","Ploughed fields"],"why":"Half of it wasn't even true."},{"q":"What saying did John use about gossips?","o":["A dog that will fetch a bone will carry a bone","The early bird catches the worm","Go to the ant","Rome wasn't built in a day"],"why":"They'll gossip about you too."},{"q":"What did John compare gossip to?","o":["A fire","Water","A song","A cake"],"why":"One spark, and the whole village burns."},{"q":"What does Proverbs 26:20 say happens with no wood?","o":["The fire goes out","The fire spreads","It rains","It gets cold"],"why":"No talebearer, no strife."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb compare words to?","o":["Eggs that break when dropped","Stones","Feathers","Water"],"why":"You can't take them back."}]},"jp3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"farm","w":"boaster","e":"big","t":"I'm the strongest man in the county! I could lift a horse with one hand! I've ploughed ten fields before breakfast!"},{"sc":"farm","w":"will","e":"shock","t":"Really? Ten fields?"},{"sc":"farm","w":"ploughman","e":"smirk","t":"Ha! Big Bragging Bill. He's all talk. The loudest drum is the emptiest one, Will. Knock on it and you'll see it's hollow."},{"sc":"farm","n":"Just then, Bill's cart got stuck in the mud. He pushed and grunted and got nowhere. A quiet old farmer walked over, put his shoulder to it, and heaved it out."},{"sc":"farm","w":"boaster","e":"worried","t":"Er... I was just about to do that..."},{"sc":"farm","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"You see, Will? People who do the most often say the least. {Tall talk} puffs you up like a balloon, and it only takes one pin to pop it."},{"sc":"farm","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"Let others praise you, if they want to. Don't do it yourself. The Bible says: let another man praise thee, and not thine own mouth."}],"quote":{"text":"Let another man praise thee, and not thine own mouth; a stranger, and not thine own lips.","who":"Proverbs 27:2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Let your work speak","text":"Big Bragging Bill talked loudly and did little. The quiet farmer said nothing and got the cart out. Boasting puffs you up and lets you down. Let your actions speak, and leave the praising to others."},"think":"Why do you think people who boast a lot often do less? How can you share good news without boasting?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Big Bragging Bill claim?","o":["He could lift a horse and plough ten fields before breakfast","He was humble","He was tired","He couldn't plough"],"why":"All talk!"},{"q":"What did John say about the loudest drum?","o":["It's the emptiest","It's the best","It's broken","It's the biggest"],"why":"Knock on it: hollow."},{"q":"Who got Bill's cart out of the mud?","o":["A quiet old farmer","Bill","Will","Mrs Chatterbox"],"why":"People who do the most say the least."},{"q":"What did John compare tall talk to?","o":["A balloon that one pin can pop","A rock","A tree","A river"],"why":"Puffed up, then popped."},{"q":"According to Proverbs 27:2, who should praise you?","o":["Another person, not your own mouth","Yourself","Nobody","Only your family"],"why":"Let your work speak."}]},"jp3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"barns","n":"Will had promised to help old Widow Jones carry her firewood on Saturday morning. But on Friday night, his friends invited him to go fishing."},{"sc":"barns","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"Mr Ploughman, do I really have to help Widow Jones? It's only firewood. Fishing will be much more fun."},{"sc":"barns","w":"ploughman","e":"stern","t":"Did you promise her, Will?"},{"sc":"barns","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"...Yes."},{"sc":"barns","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Then you have your answer. A man's word should be as good as his bond. If you say yes, mean yes. If you say no, mean no."},{"sc":"barns","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"A promise is like a seed. If you plant it and look after it, trust grows. If you break it, nothing grows, and people stop believing you."},{"sc":"barns","n":"Will helped Widow Jones on Saturday morning. She gave him a slice of her famous apple cake and told everyone in the village what a good, reliable lad he was."},{"sc":"barns","n":"Next week, the farmer down the road heard about it and offered Will a better-paid job. 'I need a lad I can trust,' he said."}],"quote":{"text":"But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.","who":"Matthew 5:37","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Yes means yes","text":"Will wanted to break a small promise for something more fun. John said: if you say yes, mean yes. Keeping your word, even when it costs you, builds trust. And trust opens doors."},"think":"Is there a promise you've made recently that you need to keep, even though it's not convenient?","quiz":[{"q":"What had Will promised?","o":["To help Widow Jones carry firewood","To go fishing","To plough a field","To buy a cake"],"why":"On Saturday morning."},{"q":"What tempted Will to break his promise?","o":["A fishing trip with friends","Sleep","Money","A party"],"why":"It seemed more fun."},{"q":"What did John compare a promise to?","o":["A seed that grows trust","A stone","A balloon","A fire"],"why":"Break it, and nothing grows."},{"q":"What happened after Will kept his word?","o":["He was offered a better job by someone who heard he was trustworthy","Nothing","He was told off","He lost his job"],"why":"Trust opens doors."},{"q":"What does Jesus say in Matthew 5:37?","o":["Let your yes be yes, and your no be no","Promises don't matter","Say maybe","Never promise"],"why":"Yea, yea; nay, nay."}]},"jp3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"grumbler","e":"frown","t":"It's too hot. Yesterday it was too wet. The bread's stale. The horses are slow. The squire's mean. Nothing's ever right!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"Grumpy Gus complained about everything. The weather. His food. His job. His neighbours. Even when things were good, he found something to moan about."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Gus, if you were in heaven, you'd complain that the harps were out of tune!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"will","e":"big","t":"Ha!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"{Grumbling} never fixed anything, Will. It doesn't make the rain stop or the sun come out. It only makes you miserable, and everyone around you too."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"When the weather's wet, I thank God for the crops. When it's dry, I thank him for the harvest. A thankful heart finds something good in every day."},{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"The Israelites in the desert grumbled about everything, even after God had rescued them from Egypt. And it kept them wandering for forty years."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"So, Will: less grumbling and more thanking. You'll be happier, and you'll be much nicer to be around!"}],"quote":{"text":"Do all things without murmurings and disputings: that ye may be blameless and harmless, the sons of God.","who":"Philippians 2:14-15","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Thank instead of grumble","text":"Grumpy Gus complained about everything, and it made everyone miserable. John Ploughman says grumbling fixes nothing. Swap grumbling for thanking. A thankful heart finds something good in every day."},"think":"Try a 'no grumbling' day. Every time you're about to complain, say something you're thankful for instead. How does it change your day?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Grumpy Gus complain about?","o":["Everything: weather, food, job and neighbours","Nothing","Only the rain","Only his horse"],"why":"Even when things were good."},{"q":"What did John joke Gus would do in heaven?","o":["Complain the harps were out of tune","Sing loudly","Fall asleep","Plough the clouds"],"why":"Ha!"},{"q":"What does grumbling fix?","o":["Nothing","The weather","The bread","Everything"],"why":"It only makes people miserable."},{"q":"How did John respond to wet weather?","o":["He thanked God for the crops","He grumbled","He stayed in bed","He moved away"],"why":"A thankful heart."},{"q":"What does Philippians 2:14 say?","o":["Do all things without murmurings","Complain often","Argue a lot","Say nothing"],"why":"No grumbling."}]}}},"jp4":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did John say a home is made of?","o":["Love","Bricks","Gold","Wood"],"why":"A house is bricks."},{"q":"When did John's family make up after quarrels?","o":["Before bedtime","Never","After a week","Next year"],"why":"Don't let the sun go down on your anger."},{"q":"Why is the young horse put next to the old horse?","o":["The old horse knows the way","For warmth","For racing","It's random"],"why":"Learn from those ahead."},{"q":"Who said 'Children, obey your parents in the Lord'?","o":["Paul, in Ephesians","John Ploughman","Noah","Moses in Genesis"],"why":"Ephesians 6:1."},{"q":"What were Will's seeds doing underground?","o":["Growing roots","Nothing","Rotting","Sleeping"],"why":"Unseen growth."},{"q":"According to the Hausa proverb, what can a patient person cook?","o":["A stone","A cloud","A tree","Iron"],"why":"And drink its soup."},{"q":"Complete: \"Let patience have her ___ work.\"","o":["perfect","slow","hard","quick"],"why":"James 1:4."},{"q":"What did John say about winters?","o":["None lasted forever","They last forever","They're always mild","He had never seen one"],"why":"Spring always comes."},{"q":"What did God promise Noah?","o":["Seedtime and harvest shall not cease","Endless summer","No more rain ever","Riches"],"why":"Genesis 8:22."},{"q":"Who wrote John Ploughman's Talk?","o":["C. H. Spurgeon","John Bunyan","George Müller","J. C. Ryle"],"why":"Spurgeon, 1869."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does Romans 15:13 ask God to fill you with?","o":["All joy and peace","Gold and silver","Fear","Food"],"why":"That ye may abound in hope."},"choices":[{"title":"A house quarrel","q":"You had a big argument with your brother. It's bedtime and you're both still angry.","o":[{"t":"Say sorry and make up before you sleep.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! John's family made up before bedtime. That's the secret."},{"t":"Ignore him for a week.","f":"Anger kept overnight grows bigger."},{"t":"Wait for him to apologise first.","f":"Someone has to go first. Why not you?"}]},{"title":"Parents say no","q":"Your parents say no to a sleepover you really wanted. You think they're being unfair.","o":[{"t":"Accept it, then calmly ask why, so you understand.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Obey with a good heart; talk respectfully when you disagree."},{"t":"Slam your door.","f":"That shows you're not ready for more freedom yet."},{"t":"Go anyway without telling them.","f":"Breaking trust makes the next 'yes' much harder."}]},{"title":"Slow progress","q":"You've been practising the keyboard for a month and you're still not very good. You want to quit.","o":[{"t":"Keep practising: the roots are growing even if you can't see it yet.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Good things grow slowly."},{"t":"Quit today.","f":"You'd be digging up the seeds before they sprout."},{"t":"Blame the teacher.","f":"Patience grows skill; blame grows nothing."}]},{"title":"A hard season","q":"Your family is going through a tough time and everything feels gloomy.","o":[{"t":"Pray, help where you can, and remember God keeps his promises.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Winter never lasts forever; spring always comes."},{"t":"Give up hope.","f":"God is the God of hope. Hold on."},{"t":"Pretend nothing is wrong and keep it all inside.","f":"Talk to God and to a trusted adult. You don't have to carry it alone."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"home","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use John Ploughman's Talk in real life."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"🏡 A home is made of love. Make up before bedtime."},{"sc":"home","n":"🧒 Learn from those who've walked the furrow before you."},{"sc":"wheatfield","n":"🌱 Good things grow slowly. Be patient."},{"sc":"valleysun","n":"🌅 Winter never lasts forever. Never lose hope."}],"stops":{"jp4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"John Ploughman's cottage was small. The roof was thatched and the floor was stone. But it was the happiest house in the village."},{"sc":"home","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"Mr Ploughman, the squire has a big house with twenty rooms. Why does yours feel happier?"},{"sc":"home","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Because a house is made of bricks, Will, but a home is made of love. A palace can be cold and a cottage can be warm."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"jpwife","e":"smile","t":"John, supper is ready! Will, you'll stay and eat with us, won't you?"},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"We pray together, we eat together, we laugh together, and when we quarrel, we make up before bedtime. That's the secret."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"And we put God at the centre. The Bible says a house is built by wisdom. When God's wisdom is the foundation, the storms can't knock it down."},{"sc":"home","n":"Will sat by the warm {hearth} and thought: one day, I want a home just like this. Not big. Just full of love."}],"quote":{"text":"Through wisdom is an house builded; and by understanding it is established: and by knowledge shall the chambers be filled with all precious and pleasant riches.","who":"Proverbs 24:3-4","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"A home is made of love","text":"John's cottage was small, but full of love. A house is made of bricks; a home is made of prayer, kindness, laughing together and making up quickly. You can help build that kind of home right now."},"think":"What is one thing you could do this week to make your home a happier place?","quiz":[{"q":"What was John Ploughman's cottage like?","o":["Small, but the happiest house in the village","Huge and cold","Empty","Made of gold"],"why":"Thatched roof, stone floor, full of love."},{"q":"What did John say a home is made of?","o":["Love","Bricks","Money","Gold"],"why":"A house is bricks; a home is love."},{"q":"What did John's family do when they quarrelled?","o":["Made up before bedtime","Stayed angry for weeks","Moved out","Never spoke again"],"why":"That's the secret."},{"q":"What did John put at the centre of his home?","o":["God","Money","The television","Work"],"why":"God's wisdom is the foundation."},{"q":"According to Proverbs 24:3, how is a house built?","o":["Through wisdom","Through money","Through luck","Through shouting"],"why":"And established by understanding."}]},"jp4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"home","w":"jpson","e":"frown","t":"Why do I have to do what Father says? I'm nearly grown up. I know what I'm doing!"},{"sc":"home","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Tom, when I plough a field, the young horse is put next to the old horse. Why? Because the old horse knows the way."},{"sc":"home","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"You'll be the old horse one day. But right now, learn from those who've walked the furrow before you."},{"sc":"home","w":"jpson","e":"worried","t":"But what if you're wrong sometimes?"},{"sc":"home","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"I will be! Fathers aren't perfect. But God put us together for a reason. Obey with a good heart, and when you disagree, talk to me respectfully. That's how you grow."},{"sc":"home","w":"ploughman","e":"stern","t":"And I tell the fathers in the village the same: lead by example. A father who shouts at his children to be patient is ploughing with a broken plough!"},{"sc":"home","w":"jpson","e":"smile","t":"All right, Father. I'll try."}],"quote":{"text":"Children, obey your parents in the Lord: for this is right. Honour thy father and mother; which is the first commandment with promise.","who":"Ephesians 6:1-2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Learn from those ahead of you","text":"The young horse learns by walking beside the old one. Obeying your parents isn't about being small; it's how you grow wise. And when you disagree, speak respectfully. That's being grown up."},"think":"How can you show respect to your parents even when you don't agree with them?","proverb":{"text":"Nwata kwọọ aka, o soro okenye rie nri.","lang":"Igbo","mean":"When a child washes his hands, he can eat with the elders. A young person who behaves well earns the respect of older people."},"quiz":[{"q":"What did Tom complain about?","o":["Having to do what his father said","Having no food","The weather","School"],"why":"He thought he was nearly grown up."},{"q":"Why is a young horse put next to an old horse?","o":["Because the old horse knows the way","To keep it warm","For company","To race it"],"why":"Learn from those who've walked the furrow."},{"q":"What did John say about fathers?","o":["They aren't perfect","They are always right","They don't matter","They never make mistakes"],"why":"But God put families together for a reason."},{"q":"What should Tom do when he disagrees?","o":["Talk respectfully","Shout","Run away","Sulk"],"why":"That's how you grow."},{"q":"What does the Igbo proverb say a child who washes his hands can do?","o":["Eat with the elders","Go out to play","Skip school","Sleep late"],"why":"Good behaviour earns respect."}]},"jp4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"wheatfield","w":"will","e":"frown","t":"I planted the seeds two weeks ago and nothing's happened! I'm going to dig them up and see what's wrong."},{"sc":"wheatfield","w":"ploughman","e":"shock","t":"Don't you dare, Will! If you dig them up, you'll kill them."},{"sc":"wheatfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Seeds need time. Under the soil, they're busy growing roots. You can't see it, but it's happening."},{"sc":"wheatfield","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Nobody can hurry the harvest. The farmer who's always pulling up his plants to look at the roots will never eat any bread."},{"sc":"wheatfield","n":"Weeks later, green shoots pushed up through the soil. By summer, the field was golden with wheat."},{"sc":"wheatfield","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"Good things grow slowly, Will: friendships, skills, a good name, and a strong faith. Have {patience}, keep working, and trust God with the timing."}],"quote":{"text":"But let patience have her perfect work, that ye may be perfect and entire, wanting nothing.","who":"James 1:4","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Good things grow slowly","text":"Will wanted to dig up his seeds because nothing was showing. But roots grow underground before shoots appear. Skills, friendships and faith grow the same way. Keep going and trust God with the timing."},"think":"What are you impatient about right now? What might be growing 'underground' that you can't see yet?","proverb":{"text":"Mai haƙuri yakan dafa dutse har ya sha romonsa.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"A patient person can cook a stone until he drinks its soup. With patience, even impossible things can be done."},"quiz":[{"q":"What did Will want to do with his seeds?","o":["Dig them up to see what was wrong","Water them","Sell them","Eat them"],"why":"He was impatient."},{"q":"What were the seeds doing underground?","o":["Growing roots","Sleeping forever","Nothing","Rotting"],"why":"You can't see it, but it's happening."},{"q":"What happened by summer?","o":["The field was golden with wheat","Nothing grew","It flooded","The birds ate everything"],"why":"Patience paid off."},{"q":"What did John say grows slowly?","o":["Friendships, skills, a good name and faith","Nothing","Only weeds","Money"],"why":"Good things take time."},{"q":"What does the Hausa proverb say a patient person can cook?","o":["A stone","Rice","An egg","Soup from water"],"why":"And drink its soup!"}]},"jp4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"night","n":"One winter, the harvest failed. Food was short and the nights were long and cold. Many in the village lost heart."},{"sc":"night","w":"will","e":"worried","t":"Mr Ploughman, what if things never get better?"},{"sc":"night","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"Will, I've seen many winters. And do you know what? Not one of them lasted forever. Spring has never missed its turn yet."},{"sc":"valleysun","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"God promised Noah: while the earth remaineth, seedtime and harvest shall not cease. He has kept that promise every single year."},{"sc":"valleysun","w":"ploughman","e":"smile","t":"That's what {hope} is. Not just wishing. It's knowing that God keeps his word. So I keep ploughing, even in the cold, because I know a harvest is coming."},{"sc":"valleysun","n":"And spring came. The fields turned green again, and the village sang at harvest time."},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"ploughman","e":"big","t":"So, Will: work hard, spend wisely, watch your tongue, love your home, be patient, and never lose hope. That's all John Ploughman has to say. God bless you!"},{"sc":"ploughfield","w":"will","e":"big","t":"Thank you, Mr Ploughman. I'll remember every word!"}],"quote":{"text":"While the earth remaineth, seedtime and harvest, and cold and heat, and summer and winter, and day and night shall not cease.","who":"Genesis 8:22","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Spring always comes","text":"When the harvest failed, John Ploughman kept hoping, because God keeps his promises. Hard times are like winter: they don't last forever. Hope is knowing God is faithful, so you keep working even in the cold."},"think":"Think of a hard 'winter' you've been through. How did spring eventually come?","quiz":[{"q":"What happened one winter?","o":["The harvest failed","It was very warm","John moved away","The squire left"],"why":"Food was short and many lost heart."},{"q":"What did John say about winters?","o":["Not one of them lasted forever","They never end","They are the best season","He liked them most"],"why":"Spring never missed its turn."},{"q":"What promise did God make to Noah?","o":["Seedtime and harvest shall not cease","It will never rain","No more winter","Everyone will be rich"],"why":"Genesis 8:22."},{"q":"What is hope, according to John?","o":["Knowing God keeps his word","Just wishing","Luck","Guessing"],"why":"Not wishing: being sure."},{"q":"Romans 15:13 calls God the God of what?","o":["Hope","Fear","Money","Winter"],"why":"Fill you with joy and peace."}]}}}});
